WEBVTT

00:08.340 --> 00:10.520
If you're done here, then leave.

00:11.550 --> 00:15.240
Would you like some, miss? It's really good.

00:16.150 --> 00:19.900
The name's Sicily. 
I'm grateful for what you've done.

00:19.900 --> 00:24.060
But we were persecuted by humans.

00:24.060 --> 00:25.950
I don't intend to be
on civil terms with you.

00:26.250 --> 00:27.600
You were persecuted?

00:27.600 --> 00:28.300
Yes.

00:28.300 --> 00:30.390
Did something happen?

00:33.590 --> 00:39.800
Numerous packs were attacked 
at once, and many kobolds died.

00:40.580 --> 00:42.530
<i>So it happened to the kobolds, too?</i>

00:42.530 --> 00:46.460
Um... Listen, aside from returning that pup,

00:46.460 --> 00:48.940
there's something I wanted to tell you.

00:50.180 --> 00:52.820
An extermination squad will be coming soon.

00:52.820 --> 00:54.450
It's dangerous to stay here.

00:55.490 --> 00:56.840
I know.

00:58.320 --> 01:00.540
The stars told us.

01:01.210 --> 01:02.370
The stars?

01:02.820 --> 01:08.050
I am a Star-Reader, a priestess able
 to read our fortune in the heavens.

01:08.050 --> 01:11.810
That must be why your name is Sicily.

01:11.810 --> 01:14.750
<i>It means "star" in Larshian.</i>

01:15.480 --> 01:17.590
We will fight with the humans.

01:18.160 --> 01:20.770
You all need to go back to your city.

01:21.340 --> 01:26.940
Um! Rather than fighting, we've thought 
up this thing called Project Shiana!

01:26.940 --> 01:29.300
So that humans and monsters
can live in harmony—

01:29.300 --> 01:30.490
I refuse.

01:30.490 --> 01:31.470
Huh?

01:32.550 --> 01:33.430
I told you.

01:34.170 --> 01:38.810
This pack is made up of kobolds 
who survived the human attacks.

01:38.810 --> 01:41.840
They rely on me as their priestess.

01:42.730 --> 01:45.160
And I've no intention of trusting humans.

01:45.770 --> 01:47.170
But...

01:47.170 --> 01:48.230
Neema!

01:48.930 --> 01:51.160
We need to head back to the city soon.

01:54.330 --> 01:57.340
Um... I'll come back tomorrow.

02:04.490 --> 02:05.930
What does this mean?

02:05.930 --> 02:09.050
The star of the savior is next to ours.

02:15.000 --> 02:18.260
Are the stars saying something interesting?

02:22.660 --> 02:25.540
Might that girl be...

02:26.540 --> 02:29.040
No, that's not possible.

02:38.800 --> 02:43.720
<b><i>Fluffy Paradise</i></b>

04:00.260 --> 04:05.220
<b><i>Episode 10   Let's Have a Strategy Meeting!</i></b>

04:00.330 --> 04:01.850
It's from Father?

04:01.850 --> 04:03.310
What does it say?

04:03.680 --> 04:06.160
Apparently, Karna is headed our way.

04:06.160 --> 04:08.720
Huh? Karna is?

04:09.030 --> 04:11.930
<i>So all three siblings will be here?
Yeah, I smell chaos.</i>

04:12.460 --> 04:15.420
And this is a local report
from the squad leader here.

04:15.940 --> 04:18.510
What did you get, Will?
The authorization you asked for?

04:18.790 --> 04:19.790
Yeah.

04:19.790 --> 04:22.900
"The prince is conducting an inspection,
 so the royal knights,

04:22.900 --> 04:27.610
regardless of station or rank,
 are to follow His Highness's orders."

04:29.000 --> 04:30.880
This is the problem, though.

04:31.870 --> 04:36.400
"In addition to carrying out a 
special inspection of the royal knights,

04:36.400 --> 04:40.250
the prince now temporarily holds
 the power to arrest."

04:40.730 --> 04:42.590
This is a royal decree from the king.

04:42.960 --> 04:43.920
Now, of all times?

04:44.190 --> 04:51.390
Yup. He's basically telling us to clean up
 any knights that might get in our way.

04:51.750 --> 04:55.610
<i>I guess Papa is really serious 
about ferreting out corruption!</i>

04:55.610 --> 04:58.510
You find this highly amusing, don't you?

04:58.510 --> 05:00.430
I-I would never!

05:02.090 --> 05:03.310
But...

05:03.690 --> 05:07.040
This means that you get to stay
with us until the end, Will!

05:09.220 --> 05:11.350
Well, as long as I'm getting results,

05:11.350 --> 05:14.000
I doubt they'll complain 
even if I'm gone awhile.

05:14.000 --> 05:17.320
Speaking of inspections,
 I wonder what happened to Healran.

05:17.320 --> 05:21.160
Hmm... I guess he never did come back.

05:21.420 --> 05:22.830
Where is he?

05:23.460 --> 05:25.600
He's hiding out in an inn in the slums?

05:25.940 --> 05:26.830
Huh?

05:26.830 --> 05:27.950
What does that mean?

05:27.950 --> 05:30.590
Who knows? That's just 
what the spirit told me.

05:31.060 --> 05:32.800
He apparently doesn't need help, though.

05:33.160 --> 05:39.190
Hmm... In that case, I'm gonna 
go back to the forest today.

05:40.100 --> 05:42.900
I brought you food, everyone!

05:45.130 --> 05:45.820
Oof!

05:47.780 --> 05:51.000
Aw, did you miss me that much, little one?

05:53.700 --> 05:55.840
Ah, so that's what you wanted.

05:55.840 --> 05:58.990
We should eat too, Gratia and Haku.
 Come on out.

05:59.680 --> 06:01.500
You really did come again.

06:01.500 --> 06:02.520
Yes.

06:04.430 --> 06:07.760
Those are... You have monsters with you?

06:08.070 --> 06:12.180
Yes. Shinki over there is a monster, too.

06:12.780 --> 06:16.470
This little slime's parent slime 
is currently inhabiting me.

06:16.790 --> 06:18.940
But why...

06:19.780 --> 06:21.660
Well, they needed help.

06:24.980 --> 06:27.320
The fact that they're with you...

06:27.320 --> 06:32.310
Is this all a part of that 
Project Shiana you mentioned?

06:32.310 --> 06:34.780
Are you interested now?

06:36.250 --> 06:43.480
It might be difficult for you to trust us 
since it was also humans that hurt you,

06:43.480 --> 06:44.400
but...

06:44.930 --> 06:47.660
I want to help you.

06:49.960 --> 06:51.100
The stars...

06:51.960 --> 06:55.630
No, I need to protect them.

06:56.330 --> 06:59.090
I need to protect the pack... 
and my little sister.

06:59.410 --> 07:01.600
You have a little sister?

07:02.240 --> 07:05.410
Yes. My entire bloodline,

07:05.410 --> 07:08.080
other than the two of us, was wiped out.

07:10.140 --> 07:15.030
Here! Try petting Haku! 
It'll help you calm down.

07:20.160 --> 07:23.040
This... has a very strange texture.

07:23.580 --> 07:26.750
It is relaxing somehow.

07:28.240 --> 07:29.200
Thank goodness.

07:30.280 --> 07:32.680
Can we save the lives of everyone here?

07:32.970 --> 07:35.750
It might be difficult to save everyone,

07:35.750 --> 07:37.630
but I'll still do all I can.

07:39.620 --> 07:42.090
Very well. Will you tell me of your plan?

07:42.640 --> 07:43.450
Right.

07:45.320 --> 07:46.770
So that's what happened?

07:47.090 --> 07:51.680
Right now, I'm gathering up monsters 
who have lost their homes

07:51.680 --> 07:54.570
and trying to find somewhere 
to relocate them.

07:55.070 --> 07:59.750
Still, I'm surprised... 
A human who saves monsters?

07:59.750 --> 08:02.310
Race and tribe don't matter.

08:02.310 --> 08:05.880
I just want to save everyone 
who's in trouble.

08:05.880 --> 08:08.360
We'll fight with you.

08:08.360 --> 08:12.220
Will you participate in this plan
 to help protect your pack?

08:14.350 --> 08:16.920
All right. I'll put my faith in you.

08:18.020 --> 08:19.400
Thank you!

08:20.360 --> 08:22.670
I will go summon the other leaders.

08:25.480 --> 08:28.480
Looks like step one was a success.

08:32.340 --> 08:34.620
<i>She said she's from a family of Star-Readers.</i>

08:34.620 --> 08:37.350
<i>I wonder if they all have different 
roles based on breed.</i>

08:37.840 --> 08:38.940
Little lady.

08:39.800 --> 08:42.600
Thank you for saving one of our pups.

08:42.600 --> 08:45.700
<i>Whoa! A super ultra fluffy floof!</i>

08:46.040 --> 08:50.410
The youngest of the Herbs is a bit careless.

08:51.140 --> 08:54.850
What? The Herbs?
 What is that bloodline about?

08:54.850 --> 08:58.090
My name is Nefertima Osphe! 
Please teach me all the things!

08:58.400 --> 09:00.000
Ah, I beg your pardon.

09:00.000 --> 09:02.440
I am from the Healer Family.
 My name is Hanley.

09:02.440 --> 09:03.890
You have a name?

09:03.890 --> 09:08.050
Oh? So you understand what 
it means for us to be named?

09:08.050 --> 09:12.540
Shinki told me about named creatures,
but I've never met one before.

09:13.450 --> 09:16.480
Is this Shinki not named?

09:16.480 --> 09:19.590
Well, I'm the one who named him.

09:19.590 --> 09:22.580
I may not look it,
 but I'm the leader of the goblins.

09:22.580 --> 09:25.010
Th-Their leader?!

09:25.010 --> 09:26.780
Yeah, it just sorta happened.

09:26.780 --> 09:29.660
Unbelievable! You're just a small child.

09:29.660 --> 09:33.620
More importantly, could you 
tell me more about kobolds?

09:34.300 --> 09:39.080
Very well. Then let me tell you 
about our ecology.

09:39.080 --> 09:40.050
Yay!

09:40.360 --> 09:46.620
First, kobold bloodlines are mainly split 
into two types: hunting and lifestyle.

09:46.620 --> 09:50.450
Hunting bloodlines excel with 
weapons and physical abilities.

09:50.450 --> 09:54.390
Lifestyle bloodlines excel at craftsmanship
and things useful in daily life.

09:55.760 --> 09:58.170
Usually, we live amongst our bloodlines,

09:58.170 --> 10:02.870
but when bloodlines come together in a pack, 
we help each other out.

10:03.200 --> 10:05.050
Excuse me, Mr. Hanley!

10:05.460 --> 10:09.690
Why do some walk on four legs 
and some walk on two?

10:09.690 --> 10:11.460
An excellent question.

10:11.460 --> 10:15.100
Once kobolds become adults, 
they're able to stand on two legs.

10:15.810 --> 10:18.240
As children, they lack the proper muscles,

10:18.240 --> 10:21.300
so they train their shoulders and 
legs by walking on all fours.

10:21.300 --> 10:22.760
Huh...

10:23.110 --> 10:26.350
For example, the range of 
motion in our joints...

10:23.450 --> 10:28.140
<i>More importantly, just look at Mr. Hanley's 
gorgeous fur. It's too hard to resist!</i>

10:33.170 --> 10:35.520
I haven't gotten floofs in forever!

10:34.830 --> 10:37.070
H-Huh? Hey, stop that!

10:37.070 --> 10:39.560
<i>He's so soft and fluffy!</i>

10:39.560 --> 10:41.440
What are you doing?

10:41.440 --> 10:42.660
Neema.

10:43.150 --> 10:47.440
Ralf, let's make a plushie of Mr. Hanley.

10:47.440 --> 10:49.700
Wh-What brought this on?

10:49.700 --> 10:53.850
He's just so fluffy! If we can recreate that,
 it's bound to be a huge hit!

10:53.850 --> 10:55.840
You're going a bit far.

10:58.930 --> 11:01.730
Ralf, why are you doing this now?

11:03.080 --> 11:04.130
This is...

11:04.130 --> 11:05.660
Yeah, I get it now.

11:05.660 --> 11:06.560
Right?!

11:06.560 --> 11:18.030
<b>fluff</b>

11:06.560 --> 11:18.030
<b>fluff</b>

11:06.560 --> 11:18.030
<b>fluff</b>

11:07.010 --> 11:12.150
But it's really delicate, so it might 
be difficult to recreate with magic.

11:13.420 --> 11:18.030
We might be able to do it if we shear him
 and use magic with no attribute.

11:18.030 --> 11:20.020
Sh-Shear me?!

11:18.030 --> 11:21.110
Yeah, we can using shaping magic 
to make the material and...

11:21.110 --> 11:23.330
That's quite enough!

11:23.330 --> 11:25.590
You will not be shearing my fur!

11:25.590 --> 11:26.070
Pardon me.

11:26.540 --> 11:28.190
Preparations are complete.

11:28.190 --> 11:29.800
Hanley, will you come with me?

11:29.800 --> 11:31.760
S-Sure...

11:32.920 --> 11:37.180
And so, the purpose of Project Shiana
 is to collect monsters.

11:37.180 --> 11:42.260
We're still looking for a location, 
but you'll be living with the goblins.

11:43.070 --> 11:47.190
I see. So every day will be
 a fight for survival.

11:47.190 --> 11:50.880
We can take the humans alive 
and use them for hunting practice.

11:50.880 --> 11:53.150
My blood's pumping now!

11:54.330 --> 11:58.480
Rather than killing them, I say we take 
advantage of the humans' dexterity.

11:58.480 --> 11:59.900
Don't you agree, Green?

12:00.300 --> 12:03.970
True. Once we settle down 
and make a huge field,

12:03.970 --> 12:05.700
we'll need some manual labor.

12:05.700 --> 12:07.730
We'd also like some help with our work.

12:07.730 --> 12:12.300
Then does that mean you 
all agree to this plan?

12:12.300 --> 12:13.220
Yes.

12:14.360 --> 12:17.920
Now we just have to figure out how 
to handle the extermination squad.

12:18.230 --> 12:20.350
Well, they've already gathered, haven't they?

12:20.350 --> 12:21.880
There's no time to evacuate.

12:22.200 --> 12:24.840
But we can't just stay here either.

12:25.130 --> 12:26.790
We'd like to avoid conflict

12:26.790 --> 12:29.810
and get to safety 
until your plan is set in motion.

12:31.530 --> 12:33.780
Why don't we face them head-on?

12:34.300 --> 12:35.490
What do you mean?

12:35.490 --> 12:39.100
We'll set upon Lenice 
with everything you've got,

12:39.100 --> 12:41.760
but then suddenly change direction.

12:41.760 --> 12:44.400
We'll use the confusion to flee west.

12:44.400 --> 12:47.190
I think we can pull it off 
with the kobolds' speed.

12:48.260 --> 12:49.650
Isn't that dangerous?

12:49.970 --> 12:52.380
We might not be able to avoid casualties.

12:52.380 --> 12:53.460
Everyone!

12:54.870 --> 12:57.490
Don't let that human fool you!

12:57.490 --> 12:59.800
Wh-Who is that?

13:01.430 --> 13:03.460
Don't let that human fool you!

13:03.740 --> 13:07.810
What are you doing here? 
The leaders are talking right now!

13:08.720 --> 13:09.900
Little Sister.

13:11.060 --> 13:12.300
<i>That's her sister?!</i>

13:12.300 --> 13:14.860
<i>She looks totally different!</i>

13:14.860 --> 13:18.730
<i>Those ears on her head and her fluffy tail...</i>

13:19.320 --> 13:21.850
Is she not a kobold?

13:21.850 --> 13:23.610
She's a beastperson, isn't she?

13:23.610 --> 13:25.560
Yes, she's from the wolf tribe.

13:26.030 --> 13:31.530
She was abandoned, so now she's
 an important member of my family.

13:31.810 --> 13:32.930
Wait.

13:32.930 --> 13:34.770
She's not from just any wolf tribe.

13:35.310 --> 13:41.000
Her fur's as dark as night, and those
 silver streaks resemble shooting stars.

13:41.580 --> 13:43.460
She's a member of the Star Wolf Tribe?

13:43.750 --> 13:47.180
I can't be certain, but I suspect
 she was born of a mutation.

13:47.760 --> 13:48.930
<i>Hmm...</i>

13:48.930 --> 13:51.320
<i>Can it really be that convenient?</i>

13:51.320 --> 13:55.560
<i>There's a possibility that God revived them.</i>

13:56.360 --> 13:57.650
<i>Which means...</i>

13:57.950 --> 14:01.860
<i>He's telling me that I must 
capture this cute little girl!</i>

14:02.800 --> 14:03.850
<i>All right.</i>

14:04.490 --> 14:05.880
Little Sister.

14:06.330 --> 14:09.280
Why do you think we're tricking you?

14:09.600 --> 14:11.600
Humans are all the same!

14:11.600 --> 14:13.430
You're greedy and cruel...

14:13.430 --> 14:16.370
You're the reason
 we're all suffering right now!

14:16.370 --> 14:19.290
It's true that the food may be a trap.

14:19.730 --> 14:21.950
Should we trust them so easily?

14:21.950 --> 14:23.230
Watch your mouth!

14:24.990 --> 14:30.050
I can't deny there are humans like that,
 but we came to help your pack.

14:30.050 --> 14:30.870
You're lying.

14:30.870 --> 14:32.090
We're not, though.

14:32.090 --> 14:36.850
If you have an idea about how 
to save your pack, please tell me.

14:38.340 --> 14:39.570
I wouldn't know...

14:39.570 --> 14:41.390
What do you mean?

14:42.150 --> 14:46.350
Well, they don't tell me 
anything because I'm a kid.

14:46.860 --> 14:51.370
But they go and tell a human who shows up
out of nowhere everything about us?

14:51.370 --> 14:52.690
That's...

14:53.840 --> 14:56.170
Just say what's on your mind.

14:56.170 --> 14:57.350
I...

14:58.020 --> 15:00.240
I can fight, too!

15:00.240 --> 15:03.210
I can defeat the humans, too!

15:03.210 --> 15:05.880
I... I...

15:05.880 --> 15:08.660
I want to do something for our pack, too...

15:13.070 --> 15:15.090
<i>I see. So she felt left out.</i>

15:21.050 --> 15:24.220
Then, hey... want to join me?

15:25.050 --> 15:25.700
Huh?

15:26.000 --> 15:28.660
You want to fight with your 
sister and everyone else, right?

15:31.610 --> 15:36.210
Still, I can understand
 why your sister is worried.

15:36.210 --> 15:40.530
So I figure you'll be safest by my side.

15:40.530 --> 15:41.450
What do you think?

15:42.370 --> 15:45.420
<i>She's really thinking about it. Meaning...</i>

15:46.880 --> 15:50.330
<i>I get to give a cute little 
girl head-pats! This is great!</i>

15:50.550 --> 15:53.830
<i>Her huge, sparkly eyes
 and her silky smooth hair...</i>

15:53.830 --> 15:55.290
<i>I just can't!</i>

15:55.570 --> 15:59.010
<b>floof</b>

15:55.720 --> 15:59.020
<i>Once we're closer, I'm gonna ask
 if I can touch her ears and tail!</i>

15:56.580 --> 15:59.010
<b>floof</b>

15:57.580 --> 15:59.010
<b>floof</b>

15:58.580 --> 15:59.010
<b>floof</b>

16:01.900 --> 16:02.940
Um...

16:04.710 --> 16:07.730
Can I really help my sister?

16:08.050 --> 16:10.940
Of course! Right?

16:14.660 --> 16:16.260
Listen well, Little Sister.

16:16.910 --> 16:18.080
Yes, Sister!

16:18.690 --> 16:21.540
That little girl is our savior.

16:21.870 --> 16:25.510
Stay by her side and protect her! Understand?

16:27.230 --> 16:28.160
Yes!

16:28.730 --> 16:29.540
What now?

16:29.540 --> 16:30.890
Hey, wait!

16:30.890 --> 16:32.800
What do you mean by savior?

16:32.800 --> 16:35.500
The stars told me that 
salvation was on the way.

16:36.020 --> 16:39.210
I'm now certain that the stars meant you.

16:39.210 --> 16:42.220
But Will and Ralf are here, too.

16:42.880 --> 16:47.400
This may sound rude, 
but if you weren't involved,

16:47.400 --> 16:50.010
I'm certain they would have given up on us.

16:50.010 --> 16:51.420
She's right.

16:51.420 --> 16:55.490
If it weren't for Neema,
 we probably never would have met.

16:55.890 --> 16:59.820
We've definitely got our hands full
 with a savior like you.

17:00.130 --> 17:02.810
Okay, let's get back to the strategy meeting.

17:13.250 --> 17:15.210
Um, Ralf...

17:16.240 --> 17:20.670
If possible, I was hoping you'd 
infiltrate the extermination squad.

17:21.010 --> 17:21.890
Why?

17:21.890 --> 17:27.730
It'd be better if we know what's going on
 with them, and you can use healing magic.

17:28.100 --> 17:30.440
I'd like to avoid any unnecessary casualties.

17:32.360 --> 17:33.030
All right.

17:34.460 --> 17:35.350
That's settled, then.

17:35.820 --> 17:37.570
Everyone, get ready.

17:37.570 --> 17:38.570
Yeah!

17:41.720 --> 17:43.500
Everyone mobile, go collect wood!

17:43.910 --> 17:47.450
Carpenter Family, get to work on the logs 
and create the carts we need to flee.

17:47.850 --> 17:50.660
Weaver and Knitter Families, 
create ropes and nets.

17:51.090 --> 17:54.630
Green and Philosopher Families, 
scout out routes for this plan.

17:54.630 --> 17:58.630
Determine where to place traps
and where to meet up after we flee.

18:00.080 --> 18:01.990
Ralf...?

18:02.590 --> 18:05.330
Using catapults would mean more firepower.

18:05.980 --> 18:09.710
They'll probably have 
five and six tag along with you.

18:10.620 --> 18:14.360
I'm the fourth-born Herb, 
the third brother. Name's Fika.

18:14.720 --> 18:17.040
What's this about tagging along with me?

18:17.040 --> 18:19.480
They'll be messengers if something happens.

18:19.480 --> 18:21.310
Ah, I see.

18:21.310 --> 18:23.950
By the way, the one you rescued...

18:24.780 --> 18:26.870
is the twelfth-born!

18:26.870 --> 18:29.410
Twelfth?! Your family's that big?!

18:30.870 --> 18:36.460
That's pretty normal. It's actually rarer 
for so many families to gather into one pack.

18:36.460 --> 18:37.620
I see.

18:38.320 --> 18:42.090
I don't know how many members 
of other packs are still alive.

18:42.450 --> 18:46.570
Maybe it'll be easier to reunite with them
 if we go along with your plan!

18:47.270 --> 18:48.590
I'm looking forward to it.

18:49.600 --> 18:50.530
Yeah.

18:51.480 --> 18:53.390
<i>Reuniting with other packs?</i>

18:53.390 --> 18:57.390
<i>You mean we might end up 
with an even bigger family of doggos?!</i>

18:57.870 --> 19:02.610
<i>Ah, the fluffy, the fluff, the fluff...</i>

19:00.290 --> 19:02.610
Neema. Neema?

19:03.560 --> 19:05.260
We're done with the meeting.

19:05.850 --> 19:07.780
To serve as messengers and scouts,

19:07.780 --> 19:12.380
the Herb Family's fifth and sixth 
pups are going to tag along.

19:12.380 --> 19:13.490
See?

19:13.930 --> 19:15.960
You're right! Nice to meet you!

19:16.310 --> 19:17.570
Um...

19:17.570 --> 19:20.660
<i>These aren't names. 
Nope, just Japanese numbers.</i>

19:20.660 --> 19:22.940
Gou and Roku!

19:25.640 --> 19:28.250
Okay, let's return to Lenice for now.

19:28.250 --> 19:29.020
Okay.

19:29.610 --> 19:33.060
Listen well. See how many 
are in the adventurers' forces.

19:33.470 --> 19:36.900
If you run into trouble, 
search out these people, okay?

19:39.910 --> 19:44.830
<i>Nox will act as an emergency messenger
and get in contact with my brother.</i>

19:45.100 --> 19:50.160
<b>Zzz...</b>

19:45.270 --> 19:50.160
<i>I guess Gratia won't have anything 
to do for now. She's still a baby, after all.</i>

19:50.470 --> 19:52.090
We'll head out as well.

19:52.950 --> 19:56.260
We'll infiltrate the adventurers' 
forces to collect intel.

19:56.260 --> 19:58.960
<i>Wow, those disguises are perfect!</i>

19:59.290 --> 20:00.330
We're counting on you.

20:00.330 --> 20:01.120
Right.

20:02.250 --> 20:06.000
All right, I guess we should 
visit the knighthood's post.

20:11.070 --> 20:12.700
Hail, Your Highness.

20:12.700 --> 20:15.570
You needn't be formal with me while I'm here.

20:15.570 --> 20:16.780
But...

20:16.780 --> 20:18.240
I'm just tagging along with her.

20:19.930 --> 20:24.160
More importantly, are you the one in charge
 of the kobold extermination squad?

20:24.460 --> 20:25.300
Yes.

20:25.300 --> 20:25.910
I see.

20:26.220 --> 20:28.820
There's something I'd like
to discuss with you about that.

20:30.370 --> 20:33.200
As you wish. Right this way.

20:35.790 --> 20:37.300
<i>Healran?!</i>

20:37.300 --> 20:38.120
Shh.

20:38.420 --> 20:39.460
<i>What's he doing here?</i>

20:39.460 --> 20:43.470
<i>This is the knighthood's post! 
Wait, why is he dressed like that?</i>

20:43.920 --> 20:45.860
Report at night.

20:47.030 --> 20:50.390
So, I'd like to go along with you
 to exterminate the kobolds.

20:50.760 --> 20:52.350
Wha— It's too dangerous!

20:52.650 --> 20:56.700
My father is preparing 
to send aid to the city.

20:56.700 --> 21:01.440
If I'm here and do nothing,
I'll bring shame to the Osphe family.

21:01.440 --> 21:04.770
Still, I cannot guarantee 
we'll be able to protect you.

21:05.030 --> 21:08.870
What if he sticks to the rear
 and heals the injured?

21:08.870 --> 21:12.070
You can use healing magic, Lord Ralfreed?

21:12.540 --> 21:14.280
To an intermediate level.

21:14.580 --> 21:15.850
Amazing.

21:17.240 --> 21:18.630
Very well.

21:18.630 --> 21:21.950
In that case, if we may borrow two guards,

21:21.950 --> 21:24.500
I'll allow you to join the rear line.

21:24.810 --> 21:25.700
Well?

21:25.700 --> 21:28.750
That's perfectly fine. 
We shall accompany Lord Ralf.

21:30.250 --> 21:31.300
I have guests!

21:31.580 --> 21:32.500
It's an emergency!

21:35.100 --> 21:35.850
What?

21:36.680 --> 21:39.470
Pardon, I must leave for a moment.

21:41.240 --> 21:42.270
I wonder what's up.

21:42.600 --> 21:49.310
Some knights that tried to break up a fight 
between some adventurers were injured.

21:49.310 --> 21:50.500
One of them gravely.

21:51.540 --> 21:52.590
Let's go.

21:52.590 --> 21:53.440
Yeah.

23:35.180 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.180 --> 23:40.010
<b>The Path I Chose</b>
